A||N||8||lildevil||need help with tire size on 17 in wheels.||||1||
Z||000000||lildevil||12-26-2001||06:44 PM||||My lil brother needs to now what size tires will work best on a Fiero with 17's. Its a 86 GT. Thinking 245/45-17 on the rear and 215 /45 -17's on the front. What you guys think? will it work?<P><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||12-26-2001||09:12 PM||||I am running those exact tire sizes on my 88 GT with 17x7.5 in wheels. I have no problems with rubbing, and they look great on the car!<BR>If you need more info e-mail me.<P>Rick 88<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||14
Z||000002||gggg-us||12-26-2001||09:31 PM||||Can the car be lowered any with those tires on it, or will it affect it at all?<P>------------------<BR>88 4Cyl ... Rebuilding 81 Vette Engine for it now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||G-Nasty||12-27-2001||04:00 AM||||With lowering springs my 87 GT has 235 45 17 ZR Yokohama Av520's w/ no prob. The O.Z. corsa rims did rub slightly with 245 45 17's on coil spring. I am in the process of either getting spacers or coil overs to allow the 245 (they look great)<BR>The front rims have 225 45 16's. This 16 & 17 tire combo rox. Get a lot of compliments due to the fact the car sits and looks perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000004||chester||12-27-2001||06:33 AM||||I run 245/40 17's rear and 215/40 17's up front with no probs.<P>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||12-27-2001||07:12 AM||||The way the Fiero should have come from the factory:<P>17x7" front with 215/45/17<BR>17x8" rear with 245/40/17  <P>(Note the slightly lower 40 percent profile, this coupled with the 245 width, keeps the front and rear sidewalls closer together in size. 245/45/17 is getting to be too much tyre squishing around in the rear.<P>Standard 40mm offsets should work fine on both front and rear wheels above.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||lildevil||12-27-2001||06:26 PM||||ok...so let me get this straight....<P>His car will be lowered using lowering springs so 245/40-17's will work on the back?  and 215/ 45-17 on the front?<P>this is a 86 remember not a 88<P><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||12-27-2001||06:48 PM||||Hrm, in that case, it may depend on the wheels.<P>It SHOULD still fit, but you'll be cutting it close.<P>Some 8" wheels with 245/40/17 rub in the rear on a pre-88, some do NOT. (on the same car)<P>Be prepared to jump to 235/45/17 if rubbing happens!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lildevil:<BR><B>ok...so let me get this straight....<P>His car will be lowered using lowering springs so 245/40-17's will work on the back?  and 215/ 45-17 on the front?<P>this is a 86 remember not a 88<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroshop||12-28-2001||11:20 AM||||Having installed many tires on the Fiero, here are the sizes that will fit properly.<BR>84 thru 87:<BR>front: 215/45/17<BR>rear:  235/45/17<P>88 only<BR>front: 215/45/17<BR>rear:  245/45/17<P>You may also on the 88 go to 225/45/17 on the front.<BR>The difference is that the 88 has different suspension and can have lrger tires.<BR>All these sizes will also work on lowered Fieros<P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
